    "runtimeProperties": {},
    "layoutPolicy": "Bubble binds all four actual wrappers. The native Primary depiction maps to the selected React API variant=default, not an invented primary prop. Native 22px corners, 10/12px insets, 14/20px text and 32px representative group spacing become reusable roles; the short primary text uses a Light face while longer specimens use Regular, and this reference explicitly selects Regular consistently. Native widths/heights remain text-dependent. All seven actual variant classes are described, including source-supported ghost without a separate native master. The unbound #C7E8FF tinted surface keeps its observed #0A0A0A text as a fixed pair across modes rather than inventing an unseen dark tint. Outline uses an inset stroke without increasing native intrinsic height. Reactions retain 2/6px insets, 4px gap and rounded surface; top/bottom half-overlap and 12px inline inset are explicit positioning decisions. Native passive reactions are 24px; an interactive child Button may enlarge this intrinsic surface. Speaker text is mandatory in this usage. Reaction state and native content actions belong to callers, not Bubble callbacks.",
    "variants": {
      "variant": {
        "prop": "variant",
        "attribute": "data-variant",
        "values": [
          "default",
          "secondary",
          "muted",
          "tinted",
          "outline",
          "ghost",
          "destructive"
        ]
      },
      "align": {
